      "player": "Sonnet Villain",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Interesting developments! I drew Teferi's Tutelage - a powerful mill enchantment. The opponent discarded Waker of Waves (which makes opposing creatures get -1/-0) using its cycling ability, and now has 3 lands (2 Forests, 1 Island).\n\
\n\
**Current hand:**\n\
- Belltower Sphinx (5 mana)\n\
- Capture Sphere (4 mana)\n\
- Creeping Bloodsucker (2 mana)\n\
- Swamp (land)\n\
- Teferi's Tutelage (3 mana)\n\
- Wall of Lost Thoughts (2 mana)\n\
- Wicked Guardian (4 mana)\n\
\n\
**Available mana:** 2 (Island + Thriving Moor)\n\
**Can cast:** Creeping Bloodsucker or Wall of Lost Thoughts\n\
\n\
**Strategic decision:**\n\
I should play my land first (Swamp), giving me 3 mana total. Then I need to decide what to cast:\n\
- Creeping Bloodsucker (1B): Recurring damage every turn\n\
- Wall of Lost Thoughts (1U): Mills 4 cards, defensive body\n\
- Teferi's Tutelage (2U): After playing Swamp, I'd have BBU or BUU available - this is castable!\n\
\n\
Actually, Teferi's Tutelage is VERY strong if I'm going for a mill strategy. It mills 2 cards every time I draw, AND it draws/discards when it enters. Let me check my mana after playing Swamp:\n\
- Island (U)\n\
- Thriving Moor (B or U)\n\
- Swamp (B)\n\
\n\
That's BBU or BUU or UUB. Teferi's Tutelage costs 2U, so I can cast it!\n\
\n\
Let me play Swamp first.",
