      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Excellent! The opponent is down to 17 life and only 21 cards left in library! The combo is working beautifully.\n\
\n\
Now I'm in postcombat main. My options:\n\
1. Play Island (always good)\n\
2. Cast Creeping Bloodsucker (1B) - recurring damage each upkeep\n\
3. Cast Wall of Lost Thoughts (1U) - mills 4 immediately\n\
\n\
**Strategic analysis:**\n\
The opponent has 21 cards left in library. If I can mill them aggressively, I can win by decking them before they kill me with their creatures. \n\
\n\
Wall of Lost Thoughts mills 4 cards immediately, which is very strong. That would put them at 17 cards.\n\
\n\
Creeping Bloodsucker provides recurring damage but doesn't help with the mill plan.\n\
\n\
I should play the Island first, then cast Wall of Lost Thoughts to mill 4 more cards.",
